Adam Trace Spragg <spragg@pc5.cs.ucdavis.edu> writes:
> Dylan O'Donnell <psmithnews@spod-central.org> wrote:
> : The return key is sending a ^J character to the game, that being the
> : control code for the ASCII line-feed character. Since NetHack doesn't
> : need to handle line-feeds, it interprets it literally as control-J;
> : which happens to be a command for "run south".
> 
> When I hit Enter, I just get a "Command ^J not recognized" or the
> equivalent....

You're probably using number_pad, then, in which case ^J _won't_ be
a movement command for you (its number_pad equivalent being G2).

> I press Enter to skip all the --More-- messages I don't care
> about.

Esc will skip all of them. Use with caution.

